      "explanation": "The square root symbol gives the nonnegative root, so \\(\\sqrt{u^2}=|u|\\). Since \\(x<0\\), we have \\(x-1<0\\), giving\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(x-1)^2}=|x-1|=1-x.\n\\]\nTherefore the expression is\n\\[\n\\left|x-(1-x)\\right|=|2x-1|.\n\\]\nBecause \\(2x-1<0\\), its absolute value is \\(-(2x-1)=1-2x\\). The answer is \\(\\boxed{1-2x}\\), choice B.",
      "id": "principal-root-and-signs",
